{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
  "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The False Claims Act (FCA) imposes civil liability on any person who presents false or fraudulent claims for payment to the Federal Government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, the relator\u2014petitioner Jesse Polansky\u2014fled a qui tam action alleging that respondent Executive Health Resources helped hospitals overbill Medicare."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Kagan delivered the opinion of the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0000-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Government can intervene after the seal period ends, so long as it shows good cause to do so. See \u00a7 3730(c)(3)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0000-0009",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 3730(c)(2)(A)\u2014which we'll call Subparagraph (2)(A) for short\u2014provides that \u201c[t]he Government may dismiss the action notwithstanding the objections of the [relator],\u201d so long as the relator has received notice of the motion and an opportunity for a hearing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Jesse Polansky is a doctor who worked for respondent Executive Health Resources (EHR), a company that helped hospitals bill the United States for Medicare-covered services."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "dissent) contends that the Government can make a (2)(A) motion only if it has intervened during the seal period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Federal Rule 41. Under that Rule, the Government was entitled to dismiss this qui tam action. We therefore affrm in all respects the judgment below."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The potential inconsistency of qui tam suits with Article II has been noticed for decades. See, e. g., Riley v. St. Luke's Episcopal Hospital, 252 F. 3d 749, 758\u2013775 (CA5 2001) (en banc) (Smith, J., dissenting); J. Blanch, Note, The Constitutionality of the False Claims Act's Qui Tam Provision, 16 Harv. J. L. & Pub. Pol'y 701, 736\u2013767 (1993); Constitutionality of the Qui Tam Provisions of the False Claims Act, 13 Op. OLC 207, 221\u2013224, 228\u2013232 (1989)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In short, there is good reason to suspect that Article II does not permit private relators to represent the United States' interests in FCA suits. However, even if that is true, the follow-on implications may not be as straightforward as they appear at frst glance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2238ca1e79ff267c93cd48ecb31b40a14db3f7f5382ec3ab7dd33166d6ea34a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2238ca1e79f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Therefore, I would vacate the judgment below granting the Government's motion to dismiss and remand for the Third Circuit to consider the correct disposition of that motion in light of any applicable constitutional requirements."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
